---
description: Where deterministic money-movement guards belong in this repo
globs:
  - workflow.go
  - activity.go
---

When deciding where a guard belongs, use this boundary:

A deterministic check that must prevent money movement from starting belongs
in the Workflow function, before the first `workflow.ExecuteActivity` call —
not inside an Activity, and not in the client that starts the Workflow.

Activities perform side effects. Once scheduled, their execution is recorded
in Workflow history; a guard inside an Activity cannot prevent its own
execution. The starter in `start/main.go` can be bypassed by other callers
and a rejection there leaves no Temporal audit trail.

Derive the specific check from the requirement and existing code. This rule
constrains placement only.
